# AGENTS.override.md — example (rename to AGENTS.override.md to use)

<!-- Pi loads ONE context file per directory, first match wins:
       AGENTS.override.md > AGENTS.md > AGENTS.MD > CLAUDE.md > CLAUDE.MD
     An AGENTS.override.md "replaces AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md only in the same directory".

     Typical use: a repo that carries BOTH a committed AGENTS.md (for other agents) and a local,
     gitignored CLAUDE.md with your personal orientation. Pi would load only AGENTS.md and silently
     ignore CLAUDE.md. A gitignored AGENTS.override.md lets you merge the two for Pi without touching
     either original. Add it to .gitignore. -->

# Local orientation (Pi, this machine)

Read `AGENTS.md` in this directory for the shared project orientation — it is NOT loaded
automatically while this override exists, so the essentials are repeated below.

## Essentials (from AGENTS.md)

- Owned repo: `sample-service`; sibling repos are read-only context.
- Tests: `.venv/bin/pytest tests/ -q`.
- Navigation: CodeGraph `codegraph_explore` → Serena `find_referencing_symbols` → grep.
- Human owns push / PR / merge / deploy.

## Personal additions (from the local CLAUDE.md)

- Machine role: read `data/changes/s3-sync/IDENTITY.md` before any shared write.
- Session start: `/skill:day start`.
